# Forbidden Practices

## Never Do

- `eval()`, `Function()` with user input
- `innerHTML` without sanitization
- Storing passwords in plain text
- Committing `.env` files
- Disabling TypeScript strict mode
- Disable ESLint rules without justification
- Ignoring lint errors
- Direct SQL queries without parameters
- Exposing internal errors in API responses
- Hardcoded URLs for API endpoints
- Storing tokens in localStorage (use cookies)
- Store sensitive data in localStorage
- Use `any` type (use `unknown` and narrow)
- Use `var` (use `const` or `let`)
- Mutate state directly
- Use index as React key for dynamic lists
- Use synchronous file operations in API routes
- Import directly from `@/ui/shadcn/*` — always use `@/ui` barrel instead
- Import directly from `@/features/*` sub-paths — always use `@/features` barrel
- Put business logic in `app/page.tsx` files — use `features/` instead
- Add `'use client'` to barrel files (`index.ts`) — see `.cursor/rules/use-client.mdc`
- Export internal sub-components (that receive callback props from a parent) from barrel files

## Deprecated Patterns (Legacy Code Only)

- `getServerSideProps` - use Server Components instead
- `pages/` directory - we've fully migrated to App Router
- `styled-components` / `@emotion` / MUI `sx` prop - use Tailwind CSS instead
- `moment.js` - use `Day.js` or native Intl API

## Performance Anti-patterns

- Avoid `useEffect` for data fetching (use Effector stores or effects)
- Don't create objects/arrays in render (use useMemo)
- Never fetch in client components when server fetch is possible

## Сarelessness Anti-patterns

- Avoid completing code implementation without Typescript and ESLint error checking
- Avoid creating markdown documents without checking .md files with a linter
